/*Q28. Write a Java program to demonstrate mutable string operations using both StringBuffer and StringBuilder.
The program should:
• Read a string from the user.
• Read the second string, which will be appended to the first.
• Create a StringBuffer object and append the second string to the first string. Print the result.
• Create a StringBuilder object using the updated string and reverse it. Print the result.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string.
• The second line contains another string to be appended to the first string.
Output Format:
• Print the output in the following format:
<appended_string>
<reversed_string>
Constraints:
• The input strings may contain spaces.*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class MutableStrings {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s1 = sc.nextLine();
        String s2 = sc.nextLine();
        StringBuffer buffer = new StringBuffer(s1);
        buffer.append(s2);
        System.out.println(buffer);
        StringBuilder builder = new StringBuilder(buffer.toString());
        builder.reverse();
        System.out.println(builder);
        sc.close();
    }
}
